{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 10,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to them that decree unrighteous decrees, and that write grievousness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they have prescribed;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To turn aside the needy from judgment, and to take away the right from the poor of my people, that widows may be their prey, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they may rob the fatherless!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And what will ye do in the day of visitation, and in the desolation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall come from far? to whom will ye flee for help? and where will ye leave your glory?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Without me they shall bow down under the prisoners, and they shall fall under the slain. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stretched out still.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Assyrian, the rod of my anger, and the staff in their hand is my indignation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will send him against a hypocritical nation, and against the people of my wrath will I give him a charge, to take the spoil, and to take the prey, and to tread them down like the mire of the streets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Howbeit he meaneth not so, neither doth his heart think so; but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his heart to destroy and cut off nations not a few.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he saith, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not my princes altogether kings?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not Calno as Carchemish? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not Hamath as Arpad? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not Samaria as Damascus?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As my hand hath found the kingdoms of the idols, and whose graven images excelled them of Jerusalem and of Samaria;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall I not, as I have done to Samaria and her idols, so do to Jerusalem and her idols?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore it shall come to pass, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " when the LORD hath performed his whole work upon mount Zion and on Jerusalem, I will punish the fruit of the stout heart of the king of Assyria, and the glory of his high looks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he saith, By the strength of my hand I have done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and by my wisdom; for I am prudent: and I have removed the bounds of the people, and have robbed their treasures, and I have put down the inhabitants like a valiant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And my hand hath found as a nest the riches of the people: and as one gathereth eggs ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " left, have I gathered all the earth; and there was none that moved the wing, or opened the mouth, or peeped.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall the ax boast itself against him that heweth with it? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall the saw magnify itself against him that moveth it? as if the rod should shake ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "itself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against them that lift it, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as if the staff should lift ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "itself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as if it were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no wood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore will the LORD, the LORD of hosts, send among his fat ones leanness; and under his glory he will kindle a burning like the burning of a fire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the light of Israel shall be for a fire, and his Holy One for a flame: and it shall burn and devour his thorns and his briers in one day;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And shall consume the glory of his forest, and of his fruitful field, both soul and body: and they shall be as when a standard-bearer fainteth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the rest of the trees of his forest shall be few, that a child may write them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall come to pass in that day, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the remnant of Israel, and such as have escaped of the house of Jacob, shall no more again lean upon him that smote them; but shall lean upon the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, in truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The remnant shall return, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the remnant of Jacob, to the mighty God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For though thy people Israel be as the sand of the sea, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a remnant of them shall return: the consumption decreed shall overflow with righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the Lord GOD of hosts will make a consumption, even determined, in the midst of all the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts, O my people that dwellest in Zion, be not afraid of the Assyrian: he shall smite thee with a rod, and shall lift up his staff against thee, after the manner of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For yet a very little while, and the indignation shall cease, and my anger in their destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD of hosts will raise up a scourge for him according to the slaughter of Midian at the rock of Oreb: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his rod ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon the sea, so shall he lift it up after the manner of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall come to pass in that day, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his burden shall be taken away from off thy shoulder, and his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is come to Aiath, he is passed to Migron; at Michmash he hath laid up his furniture.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have gone over the passage: they have taken up their lodging at Geba; Ramah is afraid; Gibeah of Saul hath fled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lift up thy voice, O daughter of Gallim: cause it to be heard to Laish, O poor Anathoth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Madmenah is removed; the inhabitants of Gebim gather themselves to flee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As yet shall he remain at Nob that day: he shall shake his hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "against",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the mount of the daughter of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, the LORD, the LORD of hosts will lop the bough with terror: and the high ones of stature ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hewn down, and the haughty shall be humbled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.10.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.10.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he shall cut down the thickets of the forests with iron, and Lebanon shall fall by a mighty one.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
